 500} and evaluation grid y \u2208 {-2, -1, 0, 1, 2}, generate M independent rate-one exponential samples of size n, compute centered maxima Y_n,i = max(sample_i) - log(n), and compare empirical CDF at each y to the exact finite-n CDF (1-exp(-y)/n)^n and standard Gumbel CDF exp(-exp(-y)) with preregistered Monte Carlo uncertainty bounds.", "Verify that the Python estimator est_exponential_maximum_gumbel correctly computes sample_size, maximum, centered_maximum, exact_cdf_at_centered using the support-aware formula, and gumbel_cdf_at_centered = exp(-exp(-centered_maximum)) for all replicates.", "Assess the approximation error (exact finite-n CDF minus Gumbel CDF) across the frozen grid as n increases, documenting per-design diagnostics without claiming uniform convergence or finite-n equality."], "acceptance_modes": ["research candidate may be reported with disclosed formal gaps"], "dimension_requirements": {"theory": "required", "scientific_code": "required", "empirical": "required", "formal": "not_applicable"}, "disclosure_requirements": ["do not call LLM proposals, retrieval hits, simulations, or static rows proof evidence", "report formal verification level as none, partial, or full"], "evaluation_mode": "research_eval", "formal_target_authoring_required": false, "formal_target_completion_policy": "formal gaps must remain explicit when the task-specific target is not kernel verified", "formal_evaluation_requires_formal_target_semantic_review": false, "formal_evaluation_requires_formalizer_lean_candidate": false, "independent_theory_review_required": true, "research_evaluation_requires_generated_algorithm_code": true, "research_evaluation_requires_generated_code_semantic_review": true, "research_evaluation_requires_generated_simulation_code": true, "research_evaluation_requires_executable_evaluator_source": true, "research_evaluation_requires_typed_metric_contracts": false, "recommended_research_path_frozen": true, "simulation_target_authoring_required": true, "so